c":true,"doc1":"Assemble ``instructions``, ``rules`` and ``memory_index`` for a session.","end":122,"hash":"9ca7a5780e","kind":"function","loc":28,"name":"assemble_run_context","params":[{"annotation":"str | PathLike[str]","name":"root"},{"annotation":"str | PathLike[str]","name":"cwd"},{"annotation":"str | PathLike[str] | None","default":"None","name":"home"},{"annotation":"Iterable[str | PathLike[str]]","default":"()","kind":"kwonly","name":"files_in_play"}],"qual":"assemble_run_context","returns":"RunContext","start":95,"test":false,"visibility":"public"}],"git":{"added":122,"commits":1,"dates":["2026-10-31"],"deleted":0,"first":"2026-10-31","last":"2026-10-31"},"lang":"python","lines":122,"module_doc":"m2c/src/m2c/context/__init__.py -- Patch C12: instructions, rules and memory.\n\nThis package prepares the three context fields of a ``run.start`` message\n(protocol/v1/run.start.json) from what is on this device:\n\n    instructions.py   M2C.md / AGENTS.md / CLAUDE.md, hierarchical, with @imports\n    rules.py          path-scoped rules from .m2c/rules/*.md\n    memory.py         the project's auto-memory index, and memory writes the\n                      user approves first (never containing secrets)\n\n``assemble_run_context(root, cwd, home)`` calls all three and returns a\n``RunContext``; ``RunContext.run_start_fields()`` is a dict with exactly the\nkeys ``instructions``, ``rules`` and ``memory_index``, ready to be passed to\n``DeviceLink.start_run(**fields, ...)`` (C04) or merged into a ``run.resume``\nstate.  NOTHING IS SENT BY THIS PACKAGE: it reads files, and writes only\nthrough ``apply_memory_write`` after an explicit approval.\n\nHow the pieces join later (not done here)\n-----------------------------------------\n* The caller (I01's repl today, C09/I02 later) supplies ``root`` (the session's\n  project path), ``cwd`` and ``home`` (None: ``~/.m2c`` or ``M2C_HOME``).\n* ``rules`` in ``run.start`` are \"the rules matched to the files in play\".  At\n  the start of a session there are none, so only unconditional rules are sent;\n  pass ``files_in_play`` when the caller knows some (for example on a\n  ``run.resume`` with state, or a fresh run started after files were touched).\n  Sending furthe","path":"m2c/src/m2c/context/__init__.py","size":5099,"test":false},{"binary":false,"blank":74,"classes":[{"bases":[],"decorators":["dataclass(frozen=True)"],"doc":true,"doc1":"Something was skipped or cut.","end":153,"fields":[{"name":"code","type":"str"},{"name":"source","type":"str"},{"name":"message","type":"str"}],"hash":"573a95b593","loc":7,"method_names":[],"methods":0,"name":"ContextNote","qual":"ContextNote","start":147},{"bases":[],"decorators":["dataclass(frozen=True)"],"doc":false,"end":161,"fields":[{"name":"text","type":"str"},{"name":"sources","type":"tuple[str, ...]"},{"name":"imports","type":"tuple[str, ...]"},{"name":"notes","type":"tuple[ContextNote, ...]"}],"hash":"1204802151","loc":5,"method_names":[],"methods":0,"name":"InstructionsResult","qual":"InstructionsResult","start":157},{"bases":["Exception"],"decorators":[],"doc":true,"doc1":"A file cannot be used; ``code`` is one of the NOTE_* strings.","end":169,"hash":"5d9202db50","loc":6,"method_names":["__init__"],"methods":1,"name":"ContextSkip","qual":"ContextSkip","start":164},{"bases":[],"decorators":["dataclass"],"doc":false,"end":287,"fields":[{"name":"label","type":"str"},{"name":"text","type":"str"},{"name":"imports","type":"tuple[str, ...]"}],"hash":"3c727b6894","loc":4,"method_names":[],"methods":0,"name":"_Chunk","qual":"_Chunk","start":284},{"bases":[],"decorators":[],"doc":true,"doc1":"State for one ``load_instructions`` call.","end":439,"hash":"764e120839","loc":150,"method_names":["__init__","note","discover","_discovered","_truncation_marker","_expand","_expand_line","_import"],"methods":8,"name":"_Loader","qual":"_Loader","start":290}],"code":318,"comment":126,"exports":["ContextNote","ContextSkip","GLOBAL_FILE_NAMES","IMPORT_EXTENSIONS","