ual":"_fit","returns":"tuple[str, list[_Chunk]]","start":449,"test":false,"visibility":"private"},{"args":0,"async":false,"calls":[["_omitted_marker","m2c/src/m2c/context/instructions.py::_omitted_marker"],["nbytes","m2c/src/m2c/context/instructions.py::nbytes"]],"cc":4,"cc_deep":4,"code":4,"decorators":[],"doc":false,"end":457,"hash":"f73ab872c5","kind":"nested","loc":4,"name":"total","params":[],"qual":"_fit.total","returns":"int","start":454,"test":false,"visibility":"public"},{"args":6,"async":false,"calls":[["real_path","m2c/src/m2c/context/instructions.py::real_path"],["is_inside","m2c/src/m2c/context/instructions.py::is_inside"],["resolve_home","m2c/src/m2c/context/instructions.py::resolve_home"],["_Loader","m2c/src/m2c/context/instructions.py::_Loader"],["os.path.relpath",null],["os.path.join",null],["_fit","m2c/src/m2c/context/instructions.py::_fit"],["InstructionsResult","m2c/src/m2c/context/instructions.py::InstructionsResult"]],"cc":7,"cc_deep":7,"code":29,"decorators":[],"doc":true,"doc1":"Load the instruction files for a session (see the module docstring).","end":518,"hash":"913a1dc2b1","kind":"function","loc":39,"name":"load_instructions","params":[{"annotation":"str | PathLike[str]","name":"root"},{"annotation":"str | PathLike[str]","name":"cwd"},{"annotation":"str | PathLike[str] | None","default":"None","name":"home"},{"annotation":"int","default":"MAX_IMPORT_DEPTH","kind":"kwonly","name":"max_import_depth"},{"annotation":"int","default":"MAX_FILE_BYTES","kind":"kwonly","name":"max_file_bytes"},{"annotation":"int","default":"MAX_TOTAL_BYTES","kind":"kwonly","name":"max_total_bytes"}],"qual":"load_instructions","raises":["ValueError"],"returns":"InstructionsResult","start":480,"test":false,"visibility":"public"}],"git":{"added":518,"commits":1,"dates":["2026-10-31"],"deleted":0,"first":"2026-10-31","last":"2026-10-31"},"lang":"python","lines":518,"module_doc":"m2c/src/m2c/context/instructions.py -- Patch C12: hierarchical instruction files\n(M2C.md, AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md) with ``@path`` imports.\n\nWhat this produces\n------------------\n``load_instructions(root, cwd, home)`` returns the text for the ``instructions``\nfield of ``run.start`` (protocol/v1/run.start.json), plus the list of files it\ncame from and a list of *notes* about anything that was skipped or cut.  Nothing\nis sent anywhere by this module; it only reads files (product guide section 9,\nbuild plan C12).\n\nOrder, and what \"takes precedence\" means\n----------------------------------------\nContent is concatenated from the LEAST specific source to the MOST specific:\n\n    1. the global file          <M2C home>/M2C.md   (M2C_HOME is honoured, see paths.py)\n    2. the repository root      M2C.md, then AGENTS.md, then CLAUDE.md\n    3. every directory below the root down to the session's working directory,\n       each with the same three names in the same order\n\nA later block overrides an earlier one by being later (models weight what they\nread last).  Only ``M2C.md`` is read from the global directory.  Directories that\nare not on the way from the root to the cwd are never read.\n\n``@path`` imports\n-----------------\nAn import is a token ``@some/path.md`` that\n\n* is at the start of a line or follows whitespace or an opening bracket/quote\n  (so ``someone@example.com`` and URLs such as ``.../@user/x`` are not imports);\n* is not inside a fenced code block (``` or ~~~) or an inline code sp","path":"m2c/src/m2c/context/instructions.py","size":22691,"test":false},{"binary":false,"blank":68,"classes":[{"bases":["Exception"],"decorators":[],"doc":true,"doc1":"Base class of the memory-write failures.","end":118,"hash":"eba48331b3","loc":2,"method_names":[],"methods":0,"name":"MemoryWriteError","qual":"MemoryWriteError","start":117},{"bases":["MemoryWriteError","ValueError"],"decorators":[],"doc":true,"doc1":"The text looks like it contains a secret.","end":126,"hash":"af5410d0f4","loc":6,"method_names":["__init__"],"methods":1,"name":"Memory